{
  "$comment": [
    "HAND-STATED, BYTES FROM THE SERVER'S ENCODERS. WIN-272 (M4.6), clients resume without missing or double-applying state.",
    "",
    "Read by packages/platos-client/tests/v1-stream.test.ts (vitest) and packages/platos-client-py/tests/test_v1_stream.py",
    "(standard library; also collected by pytest). Each drives its own SDK's generated environmentStreams.read through a fake",
    "HTTP seam that answers connection N with connection N's `wire`, split into chunks at `byteBoundaries` (UTF-8 byte offsets,",
    "so a split can fall inside a character), and compares what the reader did PER CONNECTION: the Last-Event-ID it sent, the",
    "stream_meta it read, the kernel admission of every frame, the sequences it applied, and how that connection ended.",
    "",
    "WHERE EACH SPLIT FELL IS PINNED, NOT JUST THE CONCATENATION. A reader that re-applied frames after a reconnect, applied a",
    "torn frame, or resumed from the wrong cursor can still produce the right concatenated text in some scenario; it cannot",
    "produce the right per-connection lists.",
    "",
    "The TypeScript suite joins this file to what it describes: `wire` must equal core-api's own encodeStreamMeta /",
    "encodeSseFrame / encodeSseEvent / encodeHeartbeat output for `writes` (cut after `truncatedAfter`); every cursor must be",
    "the kernel's encodeStreamCursor(journalStreamId, seq); `journalStreamId` must follow streams.controller.ts; each",
    "connection's admissions and end must be what the kernel's admitFrame and classifyStreamEnd return; and `admissionGrid`",
    "and `endGrid` must be the kernel's answers. The Python port is checked against those two grids here."
  ],
